/// <p>QQmlListReference allows C++ programs to read from, and assign values to a QML list property in a simple and type-safe way. The main advantage over using <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistproperty.html" translate="no">QQmlListProperty</a> itself is its type erasure: QQmlListReference is not a template, but can be used for QQmlListProperties of any type. Furthermore it watches the owner object for deletion and does not allow the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistproperty.html" translate="no">QQmlListProperty</a> to be accessed anymore if its owner has been deleted.</p>
