/// <p>Not all QQmlListReferences support all operations. Methods like <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistreference.html#canAppend" translate="no">canAppend</a>(), <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistreference.html#canAt" translate="no">canAt</a>(), <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistreference.html#canClear" translate="no">canClear</a>(), and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistreference.html#canCount" translate="no">canCount</a>() allow programs to query whether an operation is supported on a given property. The availability of the methods depends on the methods implemented by the underlying <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistproperty.html" translate="no">QQmlListProperty</a>. When constructing a <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qqmllistproperty.html" translate="no">QQmlListProperty</a> by manually passing the accessor functions you can restrict access to the list by passing nullptr to some of them. QQmlListReference will recognize those and report them as unavailable.</p>
